  "notes": [
    "X25519 private keys are the RAW 32 random bytes from nacl.box.keyPair() (not pre-clamped); clamping happens inside scalarMult. CryptoKit Curve25519.KeyAgreement.PrivateKey(rawRepresentation:) and libsodium accept the same bytes.",
    "Ed25519 \"private key\" on the wire/Keychain is tweetnacl's 64-byte secretKey = seed(32) || publicKey(32). CryptoKit/BouncyCastle want the 32-byte seed = first 32 bytes.",
    "nacl.box.before (used by crypto.ts computeSharedKey, meshCrypto computeToIdx, contactPair) is HSalsa20(key = X25519(priv, pub), in = 16 zero bytes) — NOT the raw X25519 output. The ratchet (utils/ratchet.ts dh()) and X3DH use RAW nacl.scalarMult output.",
    "decodeBase64 is STRICT: padding required, no url-safe alphabet, no whitespace/newlines (Android: use Base64.NO_WRAP, never DEFAULT). Every base64 a native client emits must be standard, padded, single-line.",
    "encodeUTF8(bytes→string) THROWS on invalid UTF-8 (incl. CESU/surrogate and overlong forms); every decrypt path catches it and returns null → the RN receiver shows a decrypt failure. Native senders must only encrypt well-formed UTF-8.",
    "getStableDeviceId (push-token device_id) = lowercase hex of 16 random bytes, persisted in the Keychain service com.mrenzo.deviceid (local partition)."
  ],
